==English==
{{wikipedia|Choir (disambiguation)}}
[[File:Evensong in York Minster.jpg|thumb|350px|right|A cathedral '''choir'''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|quer}}, {{m|enm|quere}}, from {{der|en|fro|quer}}, from {{der|en|la|chorus}}, from {{der|en|grc|χορός||company of dancers or singers}}. Modern spelling influenced by {{m|en|chorus}} and {{m+|fr|chœur}}. {{doublet|en|quire|chorus|hora}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kwaɪə(ɹ)/|a=UK|/kwa(ɹ)/|qq2=rapid speech}}<ref group="en-ref" name="PoCudzemu45" />
* {{audio|en|en-uk-choir.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/kwaɪɚ/|a=US|/kwaɹ/|qq2=rapid speech}}<ref group="en-ref" name="PoCudzemu45">Witt, Arlena [@ArlenaWitt] (1 June 2016). [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gYaKtceCCCw ''Chemistry, Chicago, chess | Po Cudzemu #45''] (Video) (in Polish). Event occurs at 6:52&ndash;7:15. Retrieved 12 November 2024 &ndash; via YouTube. Citing song as rapid example: {{cite-song|en|title=Like a Prayer|text=You're here with me, it's like a dream / Let the '''choir''' sing|year=1989|author=Madonna|artist=Madonna|album=Like a Prayer|authorlink=Madonna|lyricist=Madonna|composer=Patrick Leonard|publisher=Sire; Warner Bros.|url=https://www.lyrics.com/lyric/2734751/Like+a+Prayer|oclc=19469243|note=lead single|format=video}}</ref>
